zoe (android): Repro on Pixel 8 / Android 14: onboarding sample shows UI jank + duplicate refresh when user rotates during upload. Happens only with streaming RequestBody + coroutine adapter.

mike (sdk): rotate = config change kills activity and viewmodel recreate. Are you cancelling the Call on onDestroy/onStop?

zoe (android): we call call.cancel() in onDestroy but network still continues for a few seconds, and we sometimes see two refresh requests (two .execute() calls). UI shows progress freeze ~300-600ms during refresh.

angelo (devex): likely a combination: streaming non-repeatable body + blocking refresh on same OkHttpClient + handler.postAtFrontOfQueue for progress. When activity rotates you may create new call instance (clone) and both in-flight handlers/runnables race. Also some devices delay interrupting native sends.

mike (sdk): short fixes: 1) make RequestBody cancellation cooperative (AtomicBoolean + close source) 2) avoid blocking .execute() in Authenticator on upload client, use separate small auth client or return null from Authenticator and coalesce refresh in app layer 3) swap postAtFrontOfQueue -> post() and coalesce progress updates.

zoe (android): patch example I used:

```
AtomicBoolean cancelled = new AtomicBoolean(false);
RequestBody body = new RequestBody() {
  public void writeTo(BufferedSink sink) throws IOException {
    try (Source src = Okio.source(file)) {
      Buffer b = new Buffer();
      long r;
      while ((r = src.read(b, 8192)) != -1) {
        if (cancelled.get() || Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) throw new IOException("cancelled");
        sink.write(b, r);
      }
    }
  }
};
// from UI cancel handler: cancelled.set(true); source.close(); call.cancel(); call.timeout().cancel();
```

angelo (devex): also note: on Android 14 Handler.postAtFrontOfQueue has changed scheduling behavior in some builds; it can cause newly posted progress updates to preempt other lifecycle messages leading to ordering weirdness. Use post() + coalesce.

mike (sdk): action items: add cancellable streaming sample to onboarding app, update Kotlin coroutine adapter docs with invokeOnCancellation that closes stream + cancels timeout, and add a CI integration that rotates device during upload to catch duplicates.

